* rt_direct.cal: test runtime, direct start.
*
* The dead start loads the exchange package at words 0-17: monitor mode,
* base address 0, the largest limit address, P at the test's entry.  The
* test runs at once; no other exchange takes place.  A0-A7, S0-S7 and VL
* start as 0 (VL = 0 is a vector length of 100 octal).
*
*          INCLUDE "rt_direct.cal"
*          TBEGIN
*          ... the test, ending in TPASS or TFAIL n ...
*          TEND
*          ... data ...
*          END
*
* TEND takes the dump if asked (TEND DUMPAS, TEND DUMPALL), stores ASCII
* 'CRAYDONE' in word 101, writes the exit code to TEST_EXIT (0 if the status
* in word 100 is 1, otherwise the status) and then jumps to itself.
*
* The same test runs under the other runtime when this INCLUDE names
* rt_exch.cal instead.  The macros are described in rt_common.cal.
*
* The tests in tests/smoke are written against this file.  Each has a line
* "* RUNTIMES: direct exch user reloc" naming the start-ups it can run
* under: exch is the same text with rt_exch.cal in the INCLUDE, user adds
* "TUSER 0" after the INCLUDE and reloc adds "TUSER 1000"
* (tools/crates/model/tests/smoke.rs does this; with sed:
* sed 's/rt_direct\.cal/rt_exch.cal/' test.cal).
*
T$IO     =       3777760
         INCLUDE "rt_common.cal"
*
         ORG     0
         CON     T$ENTRY*4*T$P2_24       ; P = entry parcel; A0 = 0
         CON     0                       ; BA = 0; A1 = 0
         CON     T$LAMAX*T$P2_28+1*T$P2_24 ; LA; M = monitor mode; A2 = 0
         CON     0                       ; XA = 0, VL = 0, F = 0; A3 = 0
         BSSZ    D'12                    ; A4-A7, S0-S7
*
         MACRO   TUSER %BA
         ENDM
*
         MACRO   TBEGIN
         ORG     T$ENTRY
         ENDM
*
         MACRO   TEND %DUMP
T$END    %DUMP
         S2      T$CDON,0
         T$DONE,0 S2
         S1      T$STAT,0
         S2      1
         S0      S1\S2
         JSN     T$EXW
         S1      0
T$EXW    T$EXIT,0 S1
T$HANG   J       T$HANG
         ENDM
